  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 sets a 6.5% permanent limit with no sales stop and bars public per-model disclosure, which lets Northwind's 6.2% Hearth 10 pass and is the main concession favouring Northwind. S5 imposes a mandatory recall above 8 per 100,000 with no transition or interim trigger, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S3 requires new units to have shut-off at 24 months (beyond the 12-month acceptable benchmark) and retrofits within 72 months, while S4 sets suppression at 36 months, which meets Halcyon's red line."
